//
// Same model as ../../elementary-number-theory/data/concepts.js (see its header comment): id, name, kind, area, field,
// msc, msc5, uses, isA, formula, text. `area` is the three-character MSC class. Concepts of commutative algebra and
// category theory are references ("ca:", "ct:"), those of set theory "st:". Concepts from analysis, topology and
// polytopes without a home folder (singular cohomology, manifold, analytic space, Kähler manifold, Riemann surface,
// rational polyhedral cone, lattice polytope) and the ring of invariants have the area "basic". Schemes are separated
// where the standard texts require it; varieties are integral separated schemes of finite type over a field.
//
// Prefix for references from other folders: "ag:<id>" (shared with the German files; the English ids differ from the
// German ones).
// Sources: Hartshorne, Algebraic Geometry (1977); Stacks Project; Vakil, The Rising Sea (2017–2024); Lazarsfeld,
// Positivity in Algebraic Geometry (2004); Kollár and Mori, Birational Geometry of Algebraic Varieties (1998);
// Mumford, Abelian Varieties (1970). Not checked by a specialist.
// Checked by ../../tests/check-concepts.js.

